WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.477
Preserve provenance all the way through the workflow.

00:00:03.477 --> 00:00:07.812
The retriever should return source identifiers and metadata.

00:00:07.812 --> 00:00:09.907
The grader should keep them.

00:00:09.907 --> 00:00:11.942
The prompt can include them.

00:00:11.942 --> 00:00:14.477
The final answer can cite them.

00:00:14.477 --> 00:00:20.871
Then a validation step can confirm that every citation maps to evidence that was actually retrieved.

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:30.247
Useful fields include a stable source I D, chunk I D, source path or U R L, and version or effective date.

00:00:30.247 --> 00:00:37.267
For example, if two policy documents disagree, the effective date may tell you which one is current.

00:00:37.845 --> 00:00:44.932
A common mistake is turning rich evidence objects into one large plain string immediately after retrieval.

00:00:44.932 --> 00:00:48.467
That makes later citation and debugging harder.

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:51.832
Keep the evidence structure as long as possible.

00:00:51.832 --> 00:00:56.490
Format it into text only when a specific model prompt needs text.
